# Wave W17-O (Route 114): impact sand — crater-road sand: pale sand with fallen stone chips scattered in the tread, grey shards the fossil hunters turn over as they pass (design-authorised: a clear connected path of pale sand running end to end, Ashfall to Comet Falls). Split from Route 111’s dunewayfloor (sand worn thin OVER stone) by the chips: here the stone lies ON the road, fallen from the sky, not under it.
